My idea is to create a Hockey Position Guide for my hockey website. The script will be located on my hockeyplayer.html page.
The purpose of the script is to help visitors learn about the three main positions in ice hockey: goalie, defender and forward.
The website will have a dropdown menu where users can select a position. Once they select a position, JavaScript will display information explaining what that player does and their responsibilities during a hockey game.
This will make my website more interactive and help beginners understand the different roles of hockey players.

The goals I want to achieve with this script are:

Improve user experience by making the website more interactive.
Help visitors understand the different hockey positions.
Allow users to select a position using a dropdown menu.
Display different information depending on the user's selection.
Make the player page more interesting and educational.
The script will use basic JavaScript features such as variables, functions, if statements and else if statements.

Task Breakdown:
Create a heading called "Hockey Position Guide".
Create a dropdown menu containing three options: goalie, defender and forward.
Allow the user to select a position from the dropdown menu.
Use JavaScript to capture the user's selection.
Use if and else if statements to check which position was selected.
Display the correct information about the selected position.
If no position is selected, display a message asking the user to choose one.
Test the script to make sure all three positions display the correct information.

